{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H2vdXAsbDyHn4dpV6WWJTD","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→\"use client\";\n     2→\n     3→import Link from \"next/link\";\n     4→import { useRouter } from \"next/navigation\";\n     5→import { useLocale, useTranslations } from \"next-intl\";\n     6→import { LoginForm } from \"@/components/login-form\";\n     7→\n     8→export function LoginPageContent() {\n     9→  const t = useTranslations(\"login\");\n    10→  const tAuth = useTranslations(\"auth\");\n    11→  const locale = useLocale();\n    12→  const router = useRouter();\n    13→\n    14→  const handleLoginSuccess = () => {\n    15→    // Redirect to home page after successful login\n    16→    router.push(`/${locale}`);\n    17→  };\n    18→\n    19→  return (\n    20→    <div className=\"flex min-h-[calc(100vh-8rem)] items-center justify-center px-4 py-12\">\n    21→      <div className=\"w-full max-w-md space-y-8\">\n    22→        <div className=\"text-center\">\n    23→          <h1 className=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight\">{t(\"title\")}</h1>\n    24→          <p className=\"mt-2 text-muted-foreground\">{t(\"subtitle\")}</p>\n    25→        </div>\n    26→\n    27→        <div className=\"rounded-lg border bg-card p-6 shadow-sm\">\n    28→          <LoginForm onSuccess={handleLoginSuccess} />\n    29→        </div>\n    30→\n    31→        <p className=\"text-center text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n    32→          {tAuth(\"noAccount\")}{\" \"}\n    33→          <Link\n    34→            href={`/${locale}/register`}\n    35→            className=\"font-medium text-primary hover:underline\"\n    36→          >\n    37→            {tAuth(\"register\")}\n    38→          </Link>\n    39→        </p>\n    40→      </div>\n    41→    </div>\n    42→  );\n    43→}\n    44→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01N8pAHwFLZBsWuE1Keb9pDN","session_id":"48c5a601-5c0d-4020-9400-055b75cedacf","uuid":"0da56f9d-9c7e-47be-ab8e-2696bc2aa08d"}
