{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N8pAHwFLZBsWuE1Keb9pDN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create my final report:\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Exploration Report\n\nI've thoroughly explored your Roundnet Next.js application. Here's a detailed analysis organized by your requested topics:\n\n---\n\n### 1. USER MODEL STRUCTURE\n\n**Location:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202000000_create_profiles_table.sql`\n\nThe user model is built using Supabase with the following structure:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE public.profiles (\n  id uuid (references auth.users, primary key)\n  full_name text (NOT NULL, UNIQUE)\n  email text (NULLABLE)\n  created_at timestamptz (default: now())\n  updated_at timestamptz (default: now())\n)\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Uses Supabase Auth's built-in `auth.users` table for authentication\n- `id` is a foreign key reference to Supabase Auth users (cascade delete)\n- `full_name` is unique and serves as the username identifier\n- Email is optional (supports users without email verification)\n- Automatic timestamp tracking with triggers\n- Case-insensitive username lookup index: `profiles_full_name_idx` on `lower(full_name)`\n\n**Row Level Security (RLS) Policies:**\n- Users can view their own profile only\n- Users can update their own profile only\n- Authenticated users can insert their own profile during registration\n- Public read access allowed for username uniqueness checks (for registration/login validation)\n\n**Automatic Triggers:**\n- `on_auth_user_created`: Automatically creates a profile entry when a user registers (extracts `full_name` from user metadata)\n- `update_profiles_updated_at`: Automatically updates `updated_at` timestamp on changes\n\n---\n\n### 2. AUTHENTICATION PATTERNS\n\n**Supabase Client Setup:**\nLocation: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/lib/supabase.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Authentication Flow:**\n\n**A. Registration (`/src/components/registration-form.tsx`):**\n- Uses React Hook Form + Zod validation\n- Validates: `fullName` (2-100 chars), optional `email`, `password` (min 8 chars), `confirmPassword`\n- Real-time username availability checking (debounced 500ms) via Supabase\n- Sign-up method: `supabase.auth.signUp()` with email/password\n- If no email provided, creates placeholder email: `{username_lowercase_underscores}@placeholder.local`\n- Email verification optional - if provided, sends email with redirect to `/auth/callback`\n\n**B. Login (`/src/components/login-form.tsx`):**\n- Flexible login: supports both username and email\n- Username detection via regex: `/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/`\n- Flow for username-based login:\n  1. Query profiles table for matching full_name\n  2. Convert username to placeholder email format\n  3. Attempt sign-in with placeholder email\n- Google OAuth integration available\n- Sign-in method: `supabase.auth.signInWithPassword()`\n- Google OAuth: `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'google' })`\n\n**C. OAuth Callback (`/src/app/auth/callback/route.ts`):**\n- Handles OAuth code exchange: `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code)`\n- Post-authentication profile check:\n  - If user has no `full_name` in profile → redirects to `/complete-profile`\n  - If user has `full_name` → redirects to home\n- Provides error handling for auth failures\n\n**D. Profile Completion (`/src/app/[locale]/complete-profile/complete-profile-content.tsx`):**\n- Required for OAuth users who don't have a username set\n- Checks authentication status (redirects to login if not authenticated)\n- Checks if profile already has username (redirects home if yes)\n- Real-time username availability checking\n- Updates profile via upsert: `supabase.from('profiles').upsert()`\n- Also updates user metadata: `supabase.auth.updateUser()`\n\n**E. Authentication State Management:**\n- Currently hardcoded to `false` in Header component (TODO to replace with actual Supabase session)\n- Should use: `supabase.auth.getUser()` or session listener\n- No centralized auth context - implemented directly in components\n\n---\n\n### 3. TEMPLATES STRUCTURE\n\n**Base Template:**\nLocation: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx`\n\n```typescript\n// Features:\n- Locale-based routing (ES/EN)\n- Header + Main Content + Footer layout\n- NextIntl provider for i18n\n- Tailwind CSS utility classes\n- Google Fonts (Geist Sans/Mono)\n```\n\n**Page Templates:**\n- `/[locale]/page.tsx` - Home page\n- `/[locale]/login/page.tsx` - Login page (wrapper)\n- `/[locale]/register/page.tsx` - Registration page (wrapper)\n- `/[locale]/complete-profile/page.tsx` - Profile completion page (wrapper)\n\n**All pages follow pattern:**\n```typescript\nexport default async function PageName({ params }: { params: Promise<{ locale: string }> }) {\n  const { locale } = await params\n  setRequestLocale(locale)\n  return <PageContent />\n}\n```\n\n**Persistent Layout Components:**\n- **Header** (`/src/components/header.tsx`): Sticky navigation with mobile menu, language switcher, auth links\n- **Footer** (`/src/components/footer.tsx`): Footer with copyright, privacy, terms, contact links\n- **Language Switcher** (`/src/components/language-switcher.tsx`): Locale switching component\n\n---\n\n### 4. FORMS HANDLING\n\n**Framework:** React Hook Form + Zod + React Hook Form Resolvers\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n**1. Form System** (`/src/components/ui/form.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// Provides these components:\n- <Form /> (FormProvider wrapper)\n- <FormField /> (Controller wrapper with context)\n- <FormItem /> (Layout wrapper with unique ID)\n- <FormLabel /> (Radix UI Label with error state)\n- <FormControl /> (Slot-based control wrapper with ARIA attributes)\n- <FormDescription /> (Helper text)\n- <FormMessage /> (Error message display)\n```\n\n**2. Input Component** (`/src/components/ui/input.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// Features:\n- Native HTML input with Tailwind styling\n- ARIA invalid state support\n- Focus ring with ring-[3px]\n- Placeholder and selection styling\n- Disabled state opacity\n- Dark mode support\n```\n\n**3. Button Component** (`/src/components/ui/button.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// CVA (Class Variance Authority) variants:\n- Variants: default, destructive, outline, secondary, ghost, link\n- Sizes: default, xs, sm, lg, icon, icon-xs, icon-sm, icon-lg\n- ARIA invalid state support\n- Focus-visible ring styling\n- SVG icon sizing\n```\n\n**4. Label Component** (`/src/components/ui/label.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// Built on Radix UI Label primitive\n// Features: group data disabled state, peer disabled state\n```\n\n**Schema Validation Pattern:**\n\nExample from Registration Form:\n```typescript\nconst createRegistrationSchema = (t: ReturnType<typeof useTranslations<\"registration\">>) =>\n  z.object({\n    fullName: z.string()\n      .min(1, t(\"errors.fullNameRequired\"))\n      .min(2, t(\"errors.fullNameMinLength\"))\n      .max(100, t(\"errors.fullNameMaxLength\")),\n    email: z.string().email(t(\"errors.emailInvalid\")).optional().or(z.literal(\"\")),\n    password: z.string().min(1, t(\"errors.passwordRequired\")).min(8, t(\"errors.passwordMinLength\")),\n    confirmPassword: z.string(),\n  })\n  .refine((data) => data.password === data.confirmPassword, {\n    message: t(\"errors.passwordsDoNotMatch\"),\n    path: [\"confirmPassword\"],\n  });\n```\n\n**Form Submission Pattern:**\n```typescript\n- useState for isSubmitting, submitError, submitSuccess\n- useForm with resolver: zodResolver(schema)\n- onSubmit handles async Supabase operations\n- Error handling with try/catch\n- Success message display\n- Form reset on success\n```\n\n**Real-time Validation Pattern:**\n- Debounced username/email availability checks (500ms delay)\n- Visual feedback: loading spinner, check mark (available), X icon (taken)\n- FormDescription color changes based on status\n- Submit button disabled during checking or if username is taken\n\n---\n\n### 5. EXISTING PROFILE-RELATED CODE\n\n**Profile Data Storage:**\n- Minimal profile data currently: `id`, `full_name`, `email`, `created_at`, `updated_at`\n- All profile queries use: `supabase.from('profiles').select(...)`\n\n**Profile Operations:**\n\n1. **Profile Check** (Registration callback):\n```typescript\nconst { data: profile } = await supabase\n  .from(\"profiles\")\n  .select(\"full_name\")\n  .eq(\"id\", sessionData.user.id)\n  .maybeSingle();\n```\n\n2. **Username Lookup** (for login):\n```typescript\nconst { data: profileData } = await supabase\n  .from(\"profiles\")\n  .select(\"id\")\n  .ilike(\"full_name\", values.identifier)\n  .maybeSingle();\n```\n\n3. **Profile Update** (complete-profile):\n```typescript\nawait supabase.from(\"profiles\").upsert({\n  id: user.id,\n  full_name: values.username,\n  email: user.email,\n});\n```\n\n**Profile Completion Logic:**\n- Required for OAuth users\n- Enforced by auth callback redirect\n- Checks exist in component useEffect\n- No dedicated profile page/management yet (TODO in header.tsx line 24)\n\n---\n\n### 6. EMAIL VERIFICATION PATTERNS\n\n**Current Implementation:**\n\n1. **Optional Email Verification:**\n```typescript\n// During registration\nemailRedirectTo: values.email ? `${window.location.origin}/auth/callback` : undefined\n```\n- If email provided: Supabase sends verification email with callback link\n- If no email: User can still register with placeholder email\n\n2. **No Email Verification Status Tracking:**\n- Profiles table has no `email_verified` or `email_verified_at` field\n- Supabase Auth stores email verification status in `auth.users.email_confirmed_at`\n- Application doesn't currently check verification status\n\n3. **Callback Handling:**\n- All auth callbacks route through `/auth/callback`\n- Extracts `code` from query params\n- Exchanges code for session via `exchangeCodeForSession(code)`\n\n**Missing Email Verification Features:**\n- No email verification status check before allowing profile access\n- No resend verification email functionality\n- No verified badge in profile\n- No email change verification\n- No email confirmation required for certain operations\n\n---\n\n### 7. API ROUTES\n\n**Location:** `/src/app/api/`\n\n**1. Username Check Route** (`/src/app/api/auth/check-username/route.ts`):\n```typescript\nGET /api/auth/check-username?username=value\n\nResponse:\n- { available: true } - username is available\n- { available: false } - username is taken\n- { error: string } - validation or server error\n\nHandles:\n- Missing username parameter\n- Minimum 2 character requirement\n- Case-insensitive lookup (ilike)\n- Table not found errors (returns available: true)\n```\n\n**2. Health Check Route** (`/src/app/api/health/route.ts`):\n- Likely used for deployment health checks\n\n---\n\n### 8. INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n)\n\n**Framework:** next-intl\n\n**Configuration:**\n- **Locales:** Spanish (es) and English (en)\n- **Default Locale:** Spanish (es)\n- **Routing:** Locale prefix in URL: `/{locale}/path`\n\n**Middleware:** (`/src/middleware.ts`)\n- Intercepts all routes except `/api`, `/auth`, `/_next`, `/_vercel`, static files\n- Matches pattern: `/((?!api|auth|_next|_vercel|.*\\\\..*).*)`\n\n**Translation Files:**\n- `/messages/en.json` - English translations\n- `/messages/es.json` - Spanish translations (not reviewed but follows same structure)\n\n**Sections:** common, nav, auth, login, completeProfile, registration, footer, home, metadata\n\n**Usage Pattern in Components:**\n```typescript\nconst t = useTranslations(\"sectionName\");\n// Then: t(\"key\") for simple strings\n// Or:   t.rich(\"key\", { component: (chunks) => <Component>{chunks}</Component> })\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/src\n├── /app\n│   ├── [locale]\n│   │   ├── layout.tsx (main layout with header/footer)\n│   │   ├── page.tsx (home page)\n│   │   ├── /login\n│   │   │   ├── page.tsx (async wrapper)\n│   │   │   └── login-content.tsx (client component)\n│   │   ├── /register\n│   │   │   ├── page.tsx (async wrapper)\n│   │   │   └── register-content.tsx (client component)\n│   │   └── /complete-profile\n│   │       ├── page.tsx (async wrapper)\n│   │       └── complete-profile-content.tsx (client component)\n│   ├── /api\n│   │   ├── /auth\n│   │   │   └── /check-username\n│   │   │       └── route.ts\n│   │   └── /health\n│   │       └── route.ts\n│   ├── /auth\n│   │   └── /callback\n│   │       └── route.ts\n│   └── globals.css\n├── /components\n│   ├── header.tsx\n│   ├── footer.tsx\n│   ├── language-switcher.tsx\n│   ├── login-form.tsx\n│   ├── registration-form.tsx\n│   ├── /ui (shadcn/radix-ui components)\n│   │   ├── button.tsx\n│   │   ├── input.tsx\n│   │   ├── label.tsx\n│   │   └── form.tsx\n├── /lib\n│   ├── supabase.ts\n│   └── utils.ts (cn() utility)\n├── /i18n\n│   ├── config.ts (locales & defaultLocale)\n│   ├── routing.ts (routing configuration)\n│   └── request.ts\n└── middleware.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. KEY TECHNOLOGIES & DEPENDENCIES\n\n**Core:**\n- Next.js 16.1.6 (App Router)\n- React 19.2.3\n- TypeScript 5\n- Tailwind CSS 4\n\n**Forms & Validation:**\n- React Hook Form 7.71.1\n- @hookform/resolvers 5.2.2\n- Zod 4.3.6\n\n**UI Components:**\n- Radix UI 1.4.3\n- class-variance-authority 0.7.1\n- lucide-react 0.563.0 (icons)\n\n**Backend & Auth:**\n- @supabase/supabase-js 2.93.3\n\n**Internationalization:**\n- next-intl 4.8.2\n\n**Utilities:**\n- clsx 2.1.1\n- tailwind-merge 3.4.0\n\n---\n\n### 11. IMPORTANT NOTES & TODOs\n\n1. **Header Component (Line 24):** TODO to replace hardcoded `isAuthenticated = false` with actual Supabase session check\n2. **No Auth Context:** Authentication state is managed per-component; should consider centralizing\n3. **Email Verification:** Not fully implemented - no status checking or enforcement\n4. **Profile Expansion:** Currently only stores username and email; ready for extension\n5. **Error Handling:** Good patterns in place; consistent across forms\n6. **Accessibility:** ARIA attributes present in form components and buttons\n\n---\n\nThis is a well-structured Next.js application with clean separation of concerns, proper form validation, and solid authentication patterns using Supabase. The codebase is ready for profile feature expansion."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ac705e7 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c5a601-5c0d-4020-9400-055b75cedacf","uuid":"2deb5396-c0d7-466c-8308-da41313ed6c5","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase to understand:\n1. The existing user model structure (fields like username, email, membership_status, registration_date)\n2. Authentication patterns used (login_required decorators, etc.)\n3. Existing templates structure and base template\n4. How forms are handled (Flask-WTF, etc.)\n5. Any existing profile-related code\n6. Email verification patterns if any exist\n\nFocus on the Flask app structure, blueprints, models, and templates.","agentId":"ac705e7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create my final report:\n\n## Comprehensive Codebase Exploration Report\n\nI've thoroughly explored your Roundnet Next.js application. Here's a detailed analysis organized by your requested topics:\n\n---\n\n### 1. USER MODEL STRUCTURE\n\n**Location:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/supabase/migrations/20260202000000_create_profiles_table.sql`\n\nThe user model is built using Supabase with the following structure:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE public.profiles (\n  id uuid (references auth.users, primary key)\n  full_name text (NOT NULL, UNIQUE)\n  email text (NULLABLE)\n  created_at timestamptz (default: now())\n  updated_at timestamptz (default: now())\n)\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Uses Supabase Auth's built-in `auth.users` table for authentication\n- `id` is a foreign key reference to Supabase Auth users (cascade delete)\n- `full_name` is unique and serves as the username identifier\n- Email is optional (supports users without email verification)\n- Automatic timestamp tracking with triggers\n- Case-insensitive username lookup index: `profiles_full_name_idx` on `lower(full_name)`\n\n**Row Level Security (RLS) Policies:**\n- Users can view their own profile only\n- Users can update their own profile only\n- Authenticated users can insert their own profile during registration\n- Public read access allowed for username uniqueness checks (for registration/login validation)\n\n**Automatic Triggers:**\n- `on_auth_user_created`: Automatically creates a profile entry when a user registers (extracts `full_name` from user metadata)\n- `update_profiles_updated_at`: Automatically updates `updated_at` timestamp on changes\n\n---\n\n### 2. AUTHENTICATION PATTERNS\n\n**Supabase Client Setup:**\nLocation: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/lib/supabase.ts`\n\n```typescript\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Authentication Flow:**\n\n**A. Registration (`/src/components/registration-form.tsx`):**\n- Uses React Hook Form + Zod validation\n- Validates: `fullName` (2-100 chars), optional `email`, `password` (min 8 chars), `confirmPassword`\n- Real-time username availability checking (debounced 500ms) via Supabase\n- Sign-up method: `supabase.auth.signUp()` with email/password\n- If no email provided, creates placeholder email: `{username_lowercase_underscores}@placeholder.local`\n- Email verification optional - if provided, sends email with redirect to `/auth/callback`\n\n**B. Login (`/src/components/login-form.tsx`):**\n- Flexible login: supports both username and email\n- Username detection via regex: `/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/`\n- Flow for username-based login:\n  1. Query profiles table for matching full_name\n  2. Convert username to placeholder email format\n  3. Attempt sign-in with placeholder email\n- Google OAuth integration available\n- Sign-in method: `supabase.auth.signInWithPassword()`\n- Google OAuth: `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'google' })`\n\n**C. OAuth Callback (`/src/app/auth/callback/route.ts`):**\n- Handles OAuth code exchange: `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code)`\n- Post-authentication profile check:\n  - If user has no `full_name` in profile → redirects to `/complete-profile`\n  - If user has `full_name` → redirects to home\n- Provides error handling for auth failures\n\n**D. Profile Completion (`/src/app/[locale]/complete-profile/complete-profile-content.tsx`):**\n- Required for OAuth users who don't have a username set\n- Checks authentication status (redirects to login if not authenticated)\n- Checks if profile already has username (redirects home if yes)\n- Real-time username availability checking\n- Updates profile via upsert: `supabase.from('profiles').upsert()`\n- Also updates user metadata: `supabase.auth.updateUser()`\n\n**E. Authentication State Management:**\n- Currently hardcoded to `false` in Header component (TODO to replace with actual Supabase session)\n- Should use: `supabase.auth.getUser()` or session listener\n- No centralized auth context - implemented directly in components\n\n---\n\n### 3. TEMPLATES STRUCTURE\n\n**Base Template:**\nLocation: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx`\n\n```typescript\n// Features:\n- Locale-based routing (ES/EN)\n- Header + Main Content + Footer layout\n- NextIntl provider for i18n\n- Tailwind CSS utility classes\n- Google Fonts (Geist Sans/Mono)\n```\n\n**Page Templates:**\n- `/[locale]/page.tsx` - Home page\n- `/[locale]/login/page.tsx` - Login page (wrapper)\n- `/[locale]/register/page.tsx` - Registration page (wrapper)\n- `/[locale]/complete-profile/page.tsx` - Profile completion page (wrapper)\n\n**All pages follow pattern:**\n```typescript\nexport default async function PageName({ params }: { params: Promise<{ locale: string }> }) {\n  const { locale } = await params\n  setRequestLocale(locale)\n  return <PageContent />\n}\n```\n\n**Persistent Layout Components:**\n- **Header** (`/src/components/header.tsx`): Sticky navigation with mobile menu, language switcher, auth links\n- **Footer** (`/src/components/footer.tsx`): Footer with copyright, privacy, terms, contact links\n- **Language Switcher** (`/src/components/language-switcher.tsx`): Locale switching component\n\n---\n\n### 4. FORMS HANDLING\n\n**Framework:** React Hook Form + Zod + React Hook Form Resolvers\n\n**Key Components:**\n\n**1. Form System** (`/src/components/ui/form.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// Provides these components:\n- <Form /> (FormProvider wrapper)\n- <FormField /> (Controller wrapper with context)\n- <FormItem /> (Layout wrapper with unique ID)\n- <FormLabel /> (Radix UI Label with error state)\n- <FormControl /> (Slot-based control wrapper with ARIA attributes)\n- <FormDescription /> (Helper text)\n- <FormMessage /> (Error message display)\n```\n\n**2. Input Component** (`/src/components/ui/input.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// Features:\n- Native HTML input with Tailwind styling\n- ARIA invalid state support\n- Focus ring with ring-[3px]\n- Placeholder and selection styling\n- Disabled state opacity\n- Dark mode support\n```\n\n**3. Button Component** (`/src/components/ui/button.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// CVA (Class Variance Authority) variants:\n- Variants: default, destructive, outline, secondary, ghost, link\n- Sizes: default, xs, sm, lg, icon, icon-xs, icon-sm, icon-lg\n- ARIA invalid state support\n- Focus-visible ring styling\n- SVG icon sizing\n```\n\n**4. Label Component** (`/src/components/ui/label.tsx`):\n```typescript\n// Built on Radix UI Label primitive\n// Features: group data disabled state, peer disabled state\n```\n\n**Schema Validation Pattern:**\n\nExample from Registration Form:\n```typescript\nconst createRegistrationSchema = (t: ReturnType<typeof useTranslations<\"registration\">>) =>\n  z.object({\n    fullName: z.string()\n      .min(1, t(\"errors.fullNameRequired\"))\n      .min(2, t(\"errors.fullNameMinLength\"))\n      .max(100, t(\"errors.fullNameMaxLength\")),\n    email: z.string().email(t(\"errors.emailInvalid\")).optional().or(z.literal(\"\")),\n    password: z.string().min(1, t(\"errors.passwordRequired\")).min(8, t(\"errors.passwordMinLength\")),\n    confirmPassword: z.string(),\n  })\n  .refine((data) => data.password === data.confirmPassword, {\n    message: t(\"errors.passwordsDoNotMatch\"),\n    path: [\"confirmPassword\"],\n  });\n```\n\n**Form Submission Pattern:**\n```typescript\n- useState for isSubmitting, submitError, submitSuccess\n- useForm with resolver: zodResolver(schema)\n- onSubmit handles async Supabase operations\n- Error handling with try/catch\n- Success message display\n- Form reset on success\n```\n\n**Real-time Validation Pattern:**\n- Debounced username/email availability checks (500ms delay)\n- Visual feedback: loading spinner, check mark (available), X icon (taken)\n- FormDescription color changes based on status\n- Submit button disabled during checking or if username is taken\n\n---\n\n### 5. EXISTING PROFILE-RELATED CODE\n\n**Profile Data Storage:**\n- Minimal profile data currently: `id`, `full_name`, `email`, `created_at`, `updated_at`\n- All profile queries use: `supabase.from('profiles').select(...)`\n\n**Profile Operations:**\n\n1. **Profile Check** (Registration callback):\n```typescript\nconst { data: profile } = await supabase\n  .from(\"profiles\")\n  .select(\"full_name\")\n  .eq(\"id\", sessionData.user.id)\n  .maybeSingle();\n```\n\n2. **Username Lookup** (for login):\n```typescript\nconst { data: profileData } = await supabase\n  .from(\"profiles\")\n  .select(\"id\")\n  .ilike(\"full_name\", values.identifier)\n  .maybeSingle();\n```\n\n3. **Profile Update** (complete-profile):\n```typescript\nawait supabase.from(\"profiles\").upsert({\n  id: user.id,\n  full_name: values.username,\n  email: user.email,\n});\n```\n\n**Profile Completion Logic:**\n- Required for OAuth users\n- Enforced by auth callback redirect\n- Checks exist in component useEffect\n- No dedicated profile page/management yet (TODO in header.tsx line 24)\n\n---\n\n### 6. EMAIL VERIFICATION PATTERNS\n\n**Current Implementation:**\n\n1. **Optional Email Verification:**\n```typescript\n// During registration\nemailRedirectTo: values.email ? `${window.location.origin}/auth/callback` : undefined\n```\n- If email provided: Supabase sends verification email with callback link\n- If no email: User can still register with placeholder email\n\n2. **No Email Verification Status Tracking:**\n- Profiles table has no `email_verified` or `email_verified_at` field\n- Supabase Auth stores email verification status in `auth.users.email_confirmed_at`\n- Application doesn't currently check verification status\n\n3. **Callback Handling:**\n- All auth callbacks route through `/auth/callback`\n- Extracts `code` from query params\n- Exchanges code for session via `exchangeCodeForSession(code)`\n\n**Missing Email Verification Features:**\n- No email verification status check before allowing profile access\n- No resend verification email functionality\n- No verified badge in profile\n- No email change verification\n- No email confirmation required for certain operations\n\n---\n\n### 7. API ROUTES\n\n**Location:** `/src/app/api/`\n\n**1. Username Check Route** (`/src/app/api/auth/check-username/route.ts`):\n```typescript\nGET /api/auth/check-username?username=value\n\nResponse:\n- { available: true } - username is available\n- { available: false } - username is taken\n- { error: string } - validation or server error\n\nHandles:\n- Missing username parameter\n- Minimum 2 character requirement\n- Case-insensitive lookup (ilike)\n- Table not found errors (returns available: true)\n```\n\n**2. Health Check Route** (`/src/app/api/health/route.ts`):\n- Likely used for deployment health checks\n\n---\n\n### 8. INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n)\n\n**Framework:** next-intl\n\n**Configuration:**\n- **Locales:** Spanish (es) and English (en)\n- **Default Locale:** Spanish (es)\n- **Routing:** Locale prefix in URL: `/{locale}/path`\n\n**Middleware:** (`/src/middleware.ts`)\n- Intercepts all routes except `/api`, `/auth`, `/_next`, `/_vercel`, static files\n- Matches pattern: `/((?!api|auth|_next|_vercel|.*\\\\..*).*)`\n\n**Translation Files:**\n- `/messages/en.json` - English translations\n- `/messages/es.json` - Spanish translations (not reviewed but follows same structure)\n\n**Sections:** common, nav, auth, login, completeProfile, registration, footer, home, metadata\n\n**Usage Pattern in Components:**\n```typescript\nconst t = useTranslations(\"sectionName\");\n// Then: t(\"key\") for simple strings\n// Or:   t.rich(\"key\", { component: (chunks) => <Component>{chunks}</Component> })\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/src\n├── /app\n│   ├── [locale]\n│   │   ├── layout.tsx (main layout with header/footer)\n│   │   ├── page.tsx (home page)\n│   │   ├── /login\n│   │   │   ├── page.tsx (async wrapper)\n│   │   │   └── login-content.tsx (client component)\n│   │   ├── /register\n│   │   │   ├── page.tsx (async wrapper)\n│   │   │   └── register-content.tsx (client component)\n│   │   └── /complete-profile\n│   │       ├── page.tsx (async wrapper)\n│   │       └── complete-profile-content.tsx (client component)\n│   ├── /api\n│   │   ├── /auth\n│   │   │   └── /check-username\n│   │   │       └── route.ts\n│   │   └── /health\n│   │       └── route.ts\n│   ├── /auth\n│   │   └── /callback\n│   │       └── route.ts\n│   └── globals.css\n├── /components\n│   ├── header.tsx\n│   ├── footer.tsx\n│   ├── language-switcher.tsx\n│   ├── login-form.tsx\n│   ├── registration-form.tsx\n│   ├── /ui (shadcn/radix-ui components)\n│   │   ├── button.tsx\n│   │   ├── input.tsx\n│   │   ├── label.tsx\n│   │   └── form.tsx\n├── /lib\n│   ├── supabase.ts\n│   └── utils.ts (cn() utility)\n├── /i18n\n│   ├── config.ts (locales & defaultLocale)\n│   ├── routing.ts (routing configuration)\n│   └── request.ts\n└── middleware.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. KEY TECHNOLOGIES & DEPENDENCIES\n\n**Core:**\n- Next.js 16.1.6 (App Router)\n- React 19.2.3\n- TypeScript 5\n- Tailwind CSS 4\n\n**Forms & Validation:**\n- React Hook Form 7.71.1\n- @hookform/resolvers 5.2.2\n- Zod 4.3.6\n\n**UI Components:**\n- Radix UI 1.4.3\n- class-variance-authority 0.7.1\n- lucide-react 0.563.0 (icons)\n\n**Backend & Auth:**\n- @supabase/supabase-js 2.93.3\n\n**Internationalization:**\n- next-intl 4.8.2\n\n**Utilities:**\n- clsx 2.1.1\n- tailwind-merge 3.4.0\n\n---\n\n### 11. IMPORTANT NOTES & TODOs\n\n1. **Header Component (Line 24):** TODO to replace hardcoded `isAuthenticated = false` with actual Supabase session check\n2. **No Auth Context:** Authentication state is managed per-component; should consider centralizing\n3. **Email Verification:** Not fully implemented - no status checking or enforcement\n4. **Profile Expansion:** Currently only stores username and email; ready for extension\n5. **Error Handling:** Good patterns in place; consistent across forms\n6. **Accessibility:** ARIA attributes present in form components and buttons\n\n---\n\nThis is a well-structured Next.js application with clean separation of concerns, proper form validation, and solid authentication patterns using Supabase. The codebase is ready for profile feature expansion."}],"totalDurationMs":72721,"totalTokens":66473,"totalToolUseCount":41,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_read_input_tokens":65997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":471},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
